        "created_at": "2013-03-09T17:32:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm just curious, if you realize that you have missed an effect during the course of gameplay, do you rewind and try try to implement the effects?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I usually do, the other day I missed two ennead inapactitated powers and didn't realize them until after the villain turn (Play the top card of the Environment Deck and shuffle the villain trash into the villain deck.&nbsp; I attempted and played the Environment Deck (chemical explosion which incapacitated 2 heroes and turned the game from sure win next turn into Phew (thank you Wrathful Retribution).&nbsp; I was then going to try to revert the shuffling and which Ennead card would be played but at that point the two incapacitated players already reshuffled their deck and we were unable to do so.&nbsp; One thing I like about cooperative games is people don't tend to complain about this, but I was just wondering how the board feels?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:33.840Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
